WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.934 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.335
is an Emmy Award-winning writer,
actor, and comedian.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:06.706
New episodes of her podcast,
"The Sarah Silverman Podcast,"

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.474 line:92%
are released on Thursdays.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
our dear friend

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sarah Silverman.
How are you, Sarah?

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:15.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, precious.
-It's so lovely --

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.049 line:92%
lovely to lay eyes on you.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do want to start
by checking in on your father.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.520 line:92%
When we last spoke in the fall

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were on the way
to dress his wound.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had hurt his foot.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
You even, I believe,
at the time, were voting

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.197
to have the foot removed,
so badly was it injured.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:34.300
-I was Team Cut It Off
because I think it would be cool

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.972
if he had a prosthetic foot, but
I was the only one on that team.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.674 line:92%
-And so he still has the foot?

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:44.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He still has the foot.
-Good.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:48.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's fair to middling,
I would say.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Does your dad
visit you in L.A.?

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:53.553 size:78% position:39%
Is it nice to see him
when he comes out?

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
He was out here,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he actually got a pacemake
put in his heart.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was out the same day.
It was, like, crazy.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.930 line:92%
But he had a couple zinger

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:07.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
he told me about
during that experience.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
He, like, went in.
The nurse came in

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:14.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
and was explaining
what was going to --

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
what the procedure
was going to be.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's like,
"Why are you telling me?

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell the doctor!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, the doctor came in
and he --

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think this is an oldie,
but he said,

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:30.156 size:84% position:42%
"Will I be able to play
the piano after this?"

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the doctor said, "Yeah,"
and he goes, "Oh, good,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I've never been abl
to play it before."

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And then --

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:41.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the -- Oh!
The anesthesiologist came in

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was like,
"No, way! No!

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:47.107
You are not putting me to sleep!
I am not falling for it!"

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the guy's like,
"Count back from 100."

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes, "No!
I'm not gonna!"

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:54.848
And then that was the last thing
he could remember.

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.349 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Having a daughter in comedy
is he very --

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:03.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
he seems like he has no sham
in sharing these jokes.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.860 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-He loves being old.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, we were at
this sandwich place we go to

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is pre-pan.
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:15.935
-And we go to this sandwich shop
that we all like,

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:19.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were there,
and these two, like,

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:23.610
huge muscle guys walked up
to my dad on their way out

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
and were like,
"Hey!" doing this to him.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.848
And then they left, and we
were like, "What was that?

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes, "Oh, when I wen
to refill my Coke,

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:34.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw those two muscle guys,
so I went over and I go,

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
'You know what?
I think I might

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
kick the [bleep]
out of one of you."

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:39.926 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
He knows that people love it
He loves being old.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I feel like
I'm really becoming him,

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:50.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
because when I walk my dog Mar
who's like this big,

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:55.308
when she walks up to people,
I always go, "Mary, attack!"

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
And I'm just like,

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That's what my dad would say,
you know?

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:02.849
It's stupid. And then, I'm also,
like, so becoming my mom.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I was in the --
I was in line at 7-Eleven,

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:08.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the kid in front of me
is like 19.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was buying, like,
Doritos and orange soda,

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:16.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, and I just can't -
And I was like, "Really?

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:20.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't get a bag of almonds
for the same price?"

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
I do think that is the kindest

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.407 line:92%
tribute we can pay our parents

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:30.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
is to just slowly
turn into them.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:30.743 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I can't believe it.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:34.414
I'm doing just everything
that made me want to die.

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:35.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're probably doing
something else

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:36.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
that your parents
did back in the day.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've heard that you have bee
spending the pandemic

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.021 line:92%
watching a lot of "Columbo."

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's so funny,
because, actually,

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:47.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was telling my dad,
"We're watching 'Columbo,'

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.528 line:92%
and he goes, "Oh, my God.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know every episode
of 'Columbo.'

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
Name one episode."
I go, "All right.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:55.835
The one with Bruce Gordon,
and he's like, "Uh, next."

00:03:55.835 --> 00:04:00.540
And I go, "Okay. Johnny Cash is,
you know, a thief."

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes --
"No, I don't. Next."

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
I must have mentioned
like eight different ones,

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.312 line:92%
he didn't know any of them

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, my boyfriend and I
have just been obsessed

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:11.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
with watching "Columbo,"
mostly me,

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:14.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I love it so much.
And then we were --

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:16.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we don't spend
every night together.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a modern woman,
and I need space.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But I was alone one night,

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I go, "I really want
to watch a 'Columbo.'

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:23.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you mind?"
And he's like,

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:24.664 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"No, I don't mind."

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:28.501
And I watched this "Columbo,
and it was a magician in it.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think Ricardo Montalban
was in it.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:35.141 line:92%
And they revealed a magic trick,

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:38.578
and I'm not a fan of magic
but I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna do this
when Rory's here."

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:44.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
So then I go,
"Pick a number from 1 to 5."

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:49.489
And he said 3, and I go,
"Look under the blender."

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:52.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
He looks under the blender
and there's a note.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:56.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
It says, "I knew
you would pick number 3."

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.765 size:81% position:41% line:92%
He was like, "No way!"

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're laughing,
and I felt pretty cool.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:04.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he goes, "What is it?
Like a psychology thing?

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like most people pick 3?"
and I go, "No."

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "What if I
picked number 1."

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Look under the stapler.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:18.951
He's like -- We were laughin
so hard because it's so dumb

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:23.189
Like, it's just leg work.
Magic is just leg work.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:28.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In general,
you're not a fan of magic?

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:31.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, no.
I don't know why.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:34.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not proud of this,
but it enrages me.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-Like, I feel like I would b

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:42.075
somebody who would, like,
burn a witch at the stake

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:43.142 size:81% position:41% line:92%
in Salem or something.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
what's wrong with me.

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:45.411 line:92%
Not that I relate to that now,

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:49.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when I feel, like, the rag
I feel when I see magic,

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know what it is.
It's not rage,

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm just like, "So what?
He learned a trick."

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:55.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But I get that's what

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
comedy is, too, so...
-Well, I think

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.992 size:75% position:38%
the difference is --
and, again, my rage

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:03.429
towards magic, I want to make it
clear, is also irrational.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:06.165 size:81% position:41%
When you see comedy,
you don't go backstage

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
to somebody after
they told a joke and say,

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.202 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"How did you do it?"

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:13.506
Because the joke, you're showing
all parts with a joke, right

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:14.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
But they might go,

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Did you think of that
in the moment?"

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:19.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
And sometimes you do,
but many times, you don't.

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:22.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
I guess that's our magic.

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:26.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Hey, you did a few --

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess not that many,
but a lot of people

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
have been trying out
how to do comedy

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:32.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
in this very dark time
for the live arts.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did a few outdoor shows.
How was it?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I've just started doing
some outdoor shows,

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's --
it's pretty cool.

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:44.437
Like, there's this one that is
like, people in lounge chairs,

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:48.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of like -- lawn chairs.
You know...

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:51.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
And with the ticket,
they get, like, an Igloo

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause there's not
wait service or anything.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:56.015 size:81% position:41%
It's kind of no-touch.
And the Igloo has --

00:06:56.015 --> 00:07:00.153
You know, we're in California so
it has beer, water, and joints

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:04.190
You know, tons of joints.
So the air is just smoky

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
with weed and --

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they give you,
like, a new mic.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:11.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
Each comic gets a cleaned mi
that they wipe down.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.766
And, you know, it's like,
you know how strippers

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
wipe down the pole,
like, in between dances?

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just really embeds,
like, reality.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:24.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you know --
Like, "Oh. Right."

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:27.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's been fun.
It's fun doing jokes

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:31.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a live crowd,
you know, and trying --

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:34.554
I've been trying this joke
and I won't even say it.

00:07:34.554 --> 00:07:35.621 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It's not really for TV.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:40.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's very dark, Holocausty
Hitlery joke,

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:41.928 line:92%
and it keeps not working.

00:07:41.928 --> 00:07:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know when you just
stay with a joke too long --

00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:46.899
Like, you're like, "Something --
It's not that it's a bad joke.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:50.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe it just needs
an 'and' or a pause."

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.838 line:92%
It's probably just heinous

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:54.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, your podcast, obviously,
you're not the first perso

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:57.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have a podcast,
but it's very unique in that

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:58.978 line:92%
Instead of interviewing people

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:02.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
your listeners
leave you voicemails.

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:06.285 line:92%
Are you enjoying this format

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:06.986 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I love it, yeah.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:10.556
People are calling in from
all over the world, you know

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:11.290 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's so cool.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:14.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like Scotland
and Finland and Sweden.

00:08:14.961 --> 00:08:18.865
You know, it's, like, places
I've never, ever, ever been.

00:08:18.865 --> 00:08:20.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it will come
as no surprise to you

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.736 size:75% position:38%
that I greatly enjoy
hearing your voice,

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:26.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
both here
and also in podcast form.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:29.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it is just a delight
to have you.

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:32.512
What are you looking at?
-I was trying to remember

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:34.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
what I was supposed to say
to that question.

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:36.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I haven't looked
at any notes.

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:38.117 line:92%
I haven't followed any notes

00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God. You really have
turned into your mother.

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:43.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I haven't even met her
but I'm guessing...

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:46.459 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:50.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can cut this out.
-No!

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:53.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes it's not that it's
specific to the question.

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:55.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes I'm just
in the moment.

00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:58.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm genuinely curious.
Don't -- This is --

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
when I interview magicians

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.475 line:92%
they don't give this much away

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:07.013
-What is it about magician
that gives them ponytails?

00:09:07.013 --> 00:09:09.649 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
